        "title": "Your Body: A Team of Systems",
        "reading": "Your body is not one machine. It is a team of eleven organ systems working together every second. The skeletal system gives you shape and protects soft organs. Muscles attach to bones and pull them to create movement. The digestive system breaks food into tiny pieces your cells can use. The respiratory system brings in oxygen and pushes out carbon dioxide. Each system has its own job, but none of them works alone.\n\nThink about running across a field. Your nervous system sends the signal to move. Your muscular and skeletal systems carry it out. Your respiratory system speeds up to bring in more oxygen, and your circulatory system pumps that oxygen to your hardworking muscles. Your skin releases sweat to cool you down. One simple action uses nearly every system at once.\n\nScientists study each system separately to understand it, but health depends on teamwork. When one system struggles, others feel it. An infection in your lungs makes your heart work harder. A broken bone needs extra nutrients from your blood to heal. Like the defenders of a castle, your body systems each guard their own wall, but they win only when they fight together. Your body runs all this teamwork without you ever giving it a thought.",
