        "title": "Energy Changes Form",
        "reading": "Energy is the ability to do work, and it never sits still. It constantly changes from one form to another. When you eat breakfast, chemical energy stored in your food becomes kinetic energy, the energy of motion, as you walk to school. When you clap, some of that motion becomes sound energy.\n\nA toaster shows several transformations at once. Electrical energy flows into the wires, which turn it into heat energy that browns the bread. Some of that heat escapes as thermal energy into the air, and the glowing wires give off a little light energy too. One kind of energy in, several kinds out.\n\nThe most famous transformation happens in a flashlight. Chemical energy stored in the battery becomes electrical energy in the circuit, which the bulb turns into light energy, plus a little heat. Every step follows the same rule: energy is never created or destroyed, only transformed.\n\nScientists track these changes with energy charts and diagrams. Drawing each step, with arrows showing what becomes what, helps you see the full path from start to finish. Once you can trace energy's journey, you can understand everything from a car engine to a thunderstorm.\n\nWatch for transformations today. When you ride a bike, your food's chemical energy becomes motion, and your brakes turn motion into heat. When lightning flashes, electrical energy becomes light, heat, and sound in an instant. Once you start looking, you will see energy changing form everywhere you go.",
